{
  "id": "28429_hisomeru",
  "headword": "ひそめる",
  "reading": "ひそめる",
  "romaji": "hisomeru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb",
  "gloss": "to furrow (brows); to knit (brows)",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to furrow; to knit (brows)",
      "explanation": "To draw the eyebrows together, typically expressing displeasure, worry, or concern. Almost always used with {眉|まゆ} as its object. Written {顰|ひそ}める in older texts, but the kanji is rare and the verb is normally written in hiragana."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28429_hisomeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{眉|まゆ}をひそめる。",
      "english": "Furrow one's brows.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28429_hisomeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{眉|まゆ}をひそめて{私|わたし}を{見|み}た。",
      "english": "He looked at me with knitted brows.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28429_hisomeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "そんな{無礼|ぶれい}な{言|い}い{方|かた}をすれば、{周|まわ}りの{人|ひと}が{眉|まゆ}をひそめるのも{当然|とうぜん}だ。",
      "english": "If you speak so rudely, it's only natural that people around you will frown in disapproval.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive ({他動詞|たどうし}). Almost always takes {眉|まゆ} (eyebrow) as its object. The idiom {眉|まゆ}をひそめる expresses silent disapproval or concern.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {眉|まゆ}をひそめる: furrow one's brows; frown in disapproval\n- {眉|まゆ}をひそめさせる: cause (someone) to frown\n- {思|おも}わず{眉|まゆ}をひそめる: unconsciously knit one's brows\n\nNOTE:\nThe same hiragana ひそめる also represents {潜|ひそ}める (to lower one's voice, to hush; as in {声|こえ}をひそめる, {息|いき}をひそめる). These are different verbs sharing a reading; context makes the meaning clear.",
